    "body": "closes #44284\n\n### changes\n- implement `reset()` on `BreakableCUDAGraph` to iterate underlying segments and reset them (including deduped `original_graph`) and clear `_break_fns`\n- in `BreakableCudaGraphBackend.cleanup()` and `FullCudaGraphBackend.cleanup()`, reset segment graphs and call `set_global_graph_memory_pool(None)` so subsequent capture passes mint fresh pool handles instead of reviving drained pools\n- invoke `device_module.empty_cache()` and `_host_emptyCache()` (when available) in `BreakableCUDAGraphCapture.__enter__` matching `torch.cuda.graph` hygiene\n- add `_host_emptyCache()` to `drop_elastic_cuda_graph_state()`\n- added cpu unit tests covering reset, recapture fresh pool minting, and capture cache hygiene\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38573092145](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38573092145)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38573092325](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38573092325)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38573092181](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38573092181)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
